# Coverage configuration.
#
# SCOPE. The 100 per cent gate covers two things, and each is measured the way it can be.
#
# 1. `model/aa_group_model.py`, the canonical model. It is hash-frozen at the release digest,
#    every cache is linked to it, and its semantics are what the manuscript, the paper and the
#    primer describe. It is pure computation with no I/O and is tested exhaustively.
#
# 2. Every script under `tools/`: the checkers, the builders, the notebook runner and the
#    reporting scripts. Most of them are command-line entry points, so the suite runs them as
#    subprocesses (`tests/test_tools_integration.py`) and also calls their functions directly
#    (`tests/test_tools_direct.py` and the per-tool test files). `patch = subprocess` makes
#    coverage follow the subprocesses and `parallel = true` keeps their data files apart; the
#    report step combines them. Lines that can only run with an external toolchain or a
#    failing operating system are marked `# pragma: no cover` at the line, with the reason.
#
# NOT in the gate: the analysis scripts under `model/` other than the canonical model
# (`morris_screen.py`, `sobol_indices.py`, `release_gate_analysis.py` and the rest). They are
# batch Monte Carlo jobs that take minutes to hours, they write hash-linked caches, and their
# bytes are frozen: each records its SHA-256 in the cache it produced, so adding a test hook or
# a `# pragma` would invalidate the cache. They are checked by the release gate, which verifies
# every cache against the script that made it and against the canonical model.
#
# The version legs on 3.11, 3.13 and 3.14 use `.coveragerc-model`, which gates the model alone,
# because they do not run the subprocess tests.
#
# `model/aa_group_model.py` cannot carry `# pragma: no cover` comments, because editing
# the file at all changes its SHA-256 and invalidates the release. The single
# unreachable line is therefore excluded by pattern below, with its justification.
[run]
branch = False
parallel = true
patch = subprocess
include =
    model/aa_group_model.py
    tools/*.py

[report]
show_missing = True
skip_covered = False
fail_under = 100
exclude_also =
    # Defensive re-check of closure after the arrival draw in simulate(). It cannot
    # execute: the loop breaks on alive.sum() == 0 before arrivals are drawn, so
    # n_after is always at least one by the time this line is reached. Verified by
    # reading model/aa_group_model.py lines 262 to 291.
    if n_after == 0 and closure_week is None:
    # Script entry points are exercised by running the module, not by importing it.
    if __name__ == .__main__.:
